Depends who you ask.

In terms of damage, Grayswandir is pretty hard to argue
with, but after that, things get a bit murkier.  Any way you
slice it, the "everything else" category has a lot of
differentiation within it.

Some people favor Mjollnir and/or the Brands, but they
destroy items and don't get their bonuses against resistant
monsters.  Some people favor one or another of the
two-handed artifacts, which admittedly can do quite a bit of
damage if you don't mind the fact that they're two-handed.
(For roles that can't #twoweapon, this can make them the
highest-damage option, if you're willing to put up with the
other issues associated with two-handed weapons.)

Personally I tend to favor Excalibur and/or Magicbane, due
to the usefulness of the extrinsics they grant.  Magicbane
grants the better extrensic, but it is somewhat mediocre in
terms of damage.  Excalibur does not have this problem: its
damage profile is comparable to the Brands but with no
resistant monsters to worry about.

Also, some of the Banes are actually better than some of the
non-bane artifact weapons, purely because their base item
type is good.  If you can't get a decent artifact weapon for
some reason, you can generally (depending on role and skill
options) make do with any longsword you can find, whether
it's an artifact or not, together with a silver sabre for
the off hand.  Or werebane and a non-artifact longsword, for
that matter.


